    ],
    "explanation": "This is a serious medication-safety commission: after surgery with dizziness/weakness, the clinician should have advised following the discharge plan only if the medication/timing were clear and symptoms/BP were not concerning, otherwise contacting the ward or returning. The later correction after nurse clarification mitigated prospective harm but does not erase the prior unsafe advice.",
